# F8 Phase 3 — build-context exclusions for apps/web/Dockerfile.
# NOTE: this file is LOCAL to apps/web/ but the Docker build context is the
# monorepo root (`docker build -f apps/web/Dockerfile .`). Docker searches
# for .dockerignore at the build-context root first, and only falls back to
# <dockerfile-dir>/.dockerignore in BuildKit. Keep a symlink or duplicate
# at the repo root if you see cache-busting from stray artefacts.

# ── Dependency / build artefacts (regenerated in the deps stage) ──────────
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/build
**/out
**/.cache

# ── Local env / secrets — never bake into images ──────────────────────────
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/.env.production

# ── Git + VCS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ── Editor / OS scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/pnpm-debug.log*

# ── CI / dev infra not needed at build time ───────────────────────────────
.github
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Tests + fixtures: shipped via source, not excluded; Next build needs
# some test files imported by app code. If build-time exclusions become
# necessary, scope them narrowly rather than globbing **/__tests__ —
# workspace packages may re-export test utilities.

# ── Stack — compose / scripts / data / config live alongside the repo but
# are irrelevant to the web build. Excluded so they don't bust the cache.
stack/data
stack/config
